(Texts held in variables are compared at run time and make the same MS_MOVE or MS_BIND call as literals.)
(The target does not exist, so the kernel refuses with ENOENT whatever the caller's privileges.)
a text called kind is "none".
a text called binding is "bind".
a text called moving is "move".
Mount "/tmp" at "/tmp/vox_751_no_such_target" with type kind with options binding.
On error print "the bind held in text variables reached mount and was refused".
Mount "/tmp" at "/tmp/vox_751_no_such_target" with type kind with options moving.
On error print "the move held in text variables reached mount and was refused".
